{"name":"Tides of Darkness","hex":"#002400","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tides","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of tide"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of tide"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tides"},{"term":"darkness","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The state of being dark; lack of light; the absolute or comparative absence of light.","The state or quality of reflecting little light, of tending to a blackish or brownish color."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/darkness"}],"entries":[{"title":"Warcraft II: Tides of Darkness","blocks":[{"text":"Warcraft II: Tides of Darkness is a fantasy real-time strategy (RTS) computer game developed by Blizzard Entertainment and released for MS-DOS and Microsoft Windows in 1995 and Mac OS in 1996 by Blizzard's parent, Davidson & Associates. A sequel to Warcraft: Orcs & Humans, the game was met with positive reviews and won most of the major PC gaming awards in 1996. In 1996, Blizzard released an expansion pack, Warcraft II: Beyond the Dark Portal, for DOS and Mac OS, and a compilation, Warcraft II: The Dark Saga, for the PlayStation and Sega Saturn. The Battle.net edition, released in 1999, included Warcraft II: Beyond the Dark Portal, provided Blizzard's online gaming service, and replaced the MS-DOS version with a Windows one."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e3/Warcraft-2-Tides-Of-Darkness-Pc.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warcraft_II%3A_Tides_of_Darkness"},{"title":"Tide","blocks":[{"text":"Tides are the periodic rise and fall of sea level resulting from the differential gravitational forces exerted primarily by the Moon and the Sun, combined with inertial effects associated with the Earth–Moon system’s orbital motion and the Earth's rotation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Tide_overview.svg/330px-Tide_overview.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tide"},{"title":"Darkness","blocks":[{"text":"Darkness is the condition resulting from a lack of illumination, or an absence of visible light."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Creation_of_Light.png/330px-Creation_of_Light.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darkness"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/3a/WC2_Tides_UI_01.png/330px-WC2_Tides_UI_01.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/3a/WC2_Tides_UI_01.png/330px-WC2_Tides_UI_01.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"In the largest area of the screen, to the right, the Orcs (the player's, in blue) attack a Human town and its defenders (red). The flaming buildings are close to collapse, and the burnt ground to their right is the remains of a razed building. This is a winter map, and the ice enables ground units to walk over the shallow part of the sea.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWC2_Tides_UI_01.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Tide_and_Moon.jpg/330px-Tide_and_Moon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Tide_and_Moon.jpg/330px-Tide_and_Moon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"In Maine (U.S.), low tide occurs roughly at moonrise and high tide with a high Moon, corresponding to the simple gravity model of two tidal bulges; at most places however, the Moon and tides have a phase shift.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATide_and_Moon.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Tide_terms.png/500px-Tide_terms.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Tide_terms.png/500px-Tide_terms.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Illustration by the course of half a month","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATide_terms.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/High_tide_sun_moon_same_side_beginning.png/120px-High_tide_sun_moon_same_side_beginning.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/High_tide_sun_moon_same_side_beginning.png/250px-High_tide_sun_moon_same_side_beginning.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/High_tide_sun_moon_same_side_beginning.png/120px-High_tide_sun_moon_same_side_beginning.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHigh_tide_sun_moon_same_side_beginning.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Low_tide_sun_moon_90_degrees.png/120px-Low_tide_sun_moon_90_degrees.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Low_tide_sun_moon_90_degrees.png/250px-Low_tide_sun_moon_90_degrees.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Low_tide_sun_moon_90_degrees.png/120px-Low_tide_sun_moon_90_degrees.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALow_tide_sun_moon_90_degrees.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/